ing. (docs cea-shipments-q2 and series cea_shipments)\n- Voltaris shipments fell 9% in Q2, the steepest drop among large makers.\n- Voltaris's share of Caldrian transformer shipments fell from 31% to 27%. Tarnwell and imports gained share.\n- Shipments trail orders by about two quarters, so the Q2 weakness is likely to carry into the second half of 2026 and into 2027.\n- Voltaris quarterly revenue (series vltg_quarterly, C$M): 905 in 2025Q3, 960 in 2025Q4, 980 in 2026Q1, then 890 in 2026Q2, a 9% sequential drop.\n\n**Implied 2027 revenue**\n- Meeting C$4.2B needs about C$1.05B per quarter. That is about 18% above the Q2 2026 level of 890, and above any quarter in the series, where the peak is 980.\n- If Q2 2026 is the run rate (890 × 4), 2027 revenue is about C$3.56B. That is roughly 15% below guidance.\n- If the share loss continues and industry shipments stay flat to slightly down, revenue falls to about C$3.4–3.5B.\n- Reaching 4.2B would need industry growth of about 8–10% in 2027, plus Voltaris regaining its 31% share. Recent data shows the opposite on both.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I only had one quarter of share and shipment data.\n- Revenue may follow price, mix or backlog rather than unit shipments.\n- Order and backlog data, which n2 is covering, could offset this.","ttft_ms":4440,"type":"result","duration_ms":25213,"uuid":"f4dc9ef5-22ac-4b8e-9ace-c72c16a4f4c4","ttft_stream_ms":3239,"time_to_request_ms":77,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":12,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":24,"tim